      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Tura</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><h3>Destination Delivery Handover for Two‑Wheeler & Motorcycle</h3>

<p>When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its final destination, the handover must be documented in a way that protects both the shipper and the receiver. The procedure is built around three pillars – a daylight condition re‑inspection, odometer verification against the LR bilty, and a signed condition sign‑off.</p>
<p>Each pillar is performed in a prescribed order, and every step is recorded to create an indisputable audit trail. The process also satisfies regulatory requirements for vehicle transport and provides evidence for insurance claims.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Inspection is carried out under natural light to eliminate shadows or artificial lighting that could hide surface damage.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The inspector compares the vehicle’s present state with the high‑resolution pickup photographs taken at the origin. These photos include all angles – front, rear, sides, and close‑ups of any pre‑existing dents, scratches, or cosmetic flaws.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Any discrepancy – new scratches, broken mirrors, or missing accessories – is noted on a condition checklist and photographed on the spot.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Both the transporter’s representative and the receiver sign the checklist before proceeding.</span></li>
    </ul>
</span></li>

<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Odometer Verification</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The odometer reading displayed on the instrument cluster is read twice to avoid transcription errors.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>This reading is cross‑checked with the mileage recorded on the LR bilty (Load Receipt cum Bill of Lading) that was generated at the point of loading.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If the reading differs by more than the allowable tolerance (usually ±5 km), the variance is investigated – possible causes include tampering, rolling, or a clerical mistake.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The verified mileage is entered on the handover form and initialed by both parties.</span></li>
    </ul>
</span></li>

<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑off</strong>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>After the visual and mileage checks, a final condition report is prepared, summarizing the vehicle’s status, any newly observed damages, and the confirmed odometer reading.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The receiver reviews the report, confirms that it matches the physical inspection, and signs the document. The transporter’s driver or agent also signs, confirming that the handover was completed as per protocol.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Both signatures are captured electronically or on paper, and a copy of the signed report is handed to the receiver while the original is retained by the logistics provider for future reference.</span></li>
    </ul>
</span></li>
</ul>

<p>By adhering to this three‑step handover, stakeholders minimize disputes, ensure accurate mileage records, and maintain a transparent chain of custody for every two‑wheeler and motorcycle delivered. The documented handover can be presented to insurers or courts, reducing the risk of costly litigation.</p></div>
