      <span style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">CARRIER INFRASTRUCTURE</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Enclosed Container Transporters vs Open Car Haulers for Bike Transportation In Tura</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When you’re planning to move a bike from Tura to another city, you’ll quickly discover that the choice between an open trailer and an enclosed containerised carrier can make all the difference. Both options can be found through local <strong>packers and movers in Tura</strong>, but the level of protection they provide varies dramatically.</p>

<p>Open trailers are the traditional, low‑cost solution. They allow you to load the bike directly onto a flatbed and secure it with straps. However, once the trailer is on the road, the bike is exposed to the elements and road debris.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Flying stones, rain, dust, and even occasional vandalism can damage the finish, paint, or mechanical components.</p>
